{"title":"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><ol><li>This is a fifteen question free-response test. Each question has exactly one integer answer.</li>\n<li>You have 80 minutes to complete the test.</li>\n<li>You will receive 15 points for each correct answer, and 0 points for each problem left unanswered or incorrect.</li>\n<li>Figures are not necessarily drawn to scale.</li>\n<li>No aids are permitted other than scratch paper, graph paper, rulers, and erasers. No calculators, smartwatches, or computing devices are allowed. No problems on the test will require the use of a calculator.</li></ol>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da95bb74f5c3b570aeabb95aadddd06d8ffd377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2 + 5x = 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is some constant, has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> as a solution. What is the other solution?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two quadrilaterals are drawn on the plane such that they share no sides. What is the maximum possible number of intersections of the boundaries of the two quadrilaterals?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even positive integers less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> that are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. What is the sum of all possible positive integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/414b21ece7188dddd7fcdfbf4eb61f61b1975767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n)_{n\\geq 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/549c1cfefd0a31b4e009be51ff431d1e8866bc9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y_n)_{n\\geq 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />  be sequences of real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/624fdc3b96c258b9385887727c7b2c3815709b9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb6cba0b5147a2a7509e70b1613f7cf93ff36936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_0 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, and, for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c42c2eb43eee732142d0ce00d94594d1edf91fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{n+1}+y_{n+1} = 2x_n + 2y_n,\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227ff03360339f8aa8686718bc09680493a3c3d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{n+1}-y_{n+1}=3x_n-3y_n.\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"16\" />\nFind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f7b2dab43c0867ce0904f5fda81948bd4211fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-pointed fork is a figure that consists of two parts: a handle that weighs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> \"skewers\" that each weigh a nonzero integer weight (in ounces). Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer such that there exists a fork with weight <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52ac5b064abbc3f58e265004e685ed103d1d3214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />  What is the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Invites5.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/Invites5.png/400px-Invites5.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/Invites5.png/600px-Invites5.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/Invites5.png/800px-Invites5.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Five friends decide to meet together for a party. However, they did not plan the party well, and at noon, every friend leaves their own house and travels to one of the other four friends' houses, chosen uniformly at random. The probability that every friend sees another friend in the house they chose can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d278803d72fcc493afb1559174a483aa7f41d143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid with nine square cells, how many ways can Jacob shade in some nonzero number of cells such that each row, column, and diagonal contains at most one shaded cell? (A diagonal is a set of squares such that their centers lie on a line that makes a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle with the sides of the grid. Note that there are more than two diagonals.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be real numbers that satisfy\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/f/78f693cb7d70dc2ab468c46ec65dfa02a6894a28.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+y)^2(20x+21y) = 12\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51ade1fc90bda866ddcf52dd53182f1338a35a35.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+y)(20x+21y)^2 = 18.\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" />\nFind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5105fd8736d04043b1f0215adb14e7f7d06c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21x+20y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204f957f90cc34dd19937e216f02c5a38663869d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=DC$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25a1e0caafcceb2a2e11c0b2373e89f639f299d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC=2\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"147\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff2219e4b6351e8b0b3b3ba2294a9133e4bf38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c68227ec2efd9339ffd16251b000f7b70017e121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0b75202202b36c2a62a22bba07fc06501bea7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen in isosceles trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b44beb78e8be18179bfb7fe6b3424e7fb1aef32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/4483542fa46123b1e899eda06f3de671df25bd07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=20$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254e7e0278f8ac462ed26c600a8bbd800b86e1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=28$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/3/ab3e775e3fa4f944039a9d682ecb0f7542f7bc33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. If the sum of the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0830febe7535fbbdf19782a978c79c0c9e6cd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249e729f8542ff5cfba842850a5efd1bc66e217e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PDA$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f550db59d15933de1a0871aaa917acdd99966af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PAB$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888fed89e19182447f85b3cb6676548a49395284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the arithmetic progression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c10e87d3aa70d3bdfcded2175ae27eaa079a631.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4,9,14,\\ldots,n\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> perfect squares. Find the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is drawn such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab757085426e6962c7d3068e5180cccf07a5cce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0938b1cb2a92765e576c16687c904efdf2cb03a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a square that contains vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in its interior. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/2627704555ddbedd1cc325a93f80bbe8760f8e36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2+CF^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an odd integer (not necessarily positive) such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975a2e4267d19cc20894011f2fda568d7533416b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{p^{n+p+2021}}{(p+n)^2}\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"44\" /> is an integer. Find the sum of all distinct possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef362837b053a94ec49129340c6732c0439aff58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\cdot n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let there be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb20df9f4016a15bd68c2c0286c8b5e540ced58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b196f83c62ce83e5cb39f4d69af59fe42401f4da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f43e3d27fe9f4d0a322db6e6d2f1f28100e7e5cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce072207ec7f3950caaa33f1b061e7082e080ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> Let the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> intersect hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99bf919578d0792af7a1f353c4ca690c7c5c030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{FC}{BF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"27\" height=\"23\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Abhishek is choosing positive integer factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef6a43520cfbac0293b191bb783f4c720a242200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2021 \\times 2^{2021}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> with replacement. After a minute passes, he chooses a random factor and writes it down. Abhishek repeats this process until the first time the product of all numbers written down is a perfect square. Find the expected number of minutes it takes for him to stop.   \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems\">2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://a